    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-email-domain rejection following the repository's existing conventions for owner-creation business rules:\n\n1. **`util/DisposableEmailDomains.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility utility holding the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) and an `isDisposable(email)` method that extracts the domain (after the last `@`) and checks it case-insensitively. This sits alongside the other email helpers like `EmailNormalizer`.\n\n2. **`service/DisposableEmailDomainException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing owner-creation exceptions (`CityCapacityExceededException`, etc.), documented as signalling a bad request.\n\n3. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 added an early guard that throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` when the (already-normalized) email domain is blocked, consistent with the other rule checks in that method.\n\n4. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping the new exception to **400 Bad Request**, following the exact `ProblemDetail`/logging pattern of the neighbouring handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (POST owner with `x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
